#. Tag: title
#: editor-filters-emboss.docbook:4
#, no-c-format
msgid "Emboss Image"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-filters-emboss.docbook:7
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &digikam; <emphasis>Emboss</emphasis> filter sculptures your image into "
"3-D as if it were stamped into wax. It uses an algorithm copyrighted by "
"Pieter Voloshyn."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editor-filters-emboss.docbook:12
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-filters-emboss.docbook:14
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &digikam; <emphasis>Emboss</emphasis> filter is a quick tool to render "
"your images in a 3-D effect. It works particularly well on images with "
"simple structure where color is not the most important content. The filter "
"uses the difference between colors and luminosity to convert it into a grey, "
"moon-like landscape lit from 10 o'clock."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editor-filters-emboss.docbook:21
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using the Emboss filter"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-filters-emboss.docbook:23
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Depth</guilabel> control allows to define the contrast of the "
"filtering. A value of 30 (10%) is the standard."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editor-filters-emboss.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Emboss filter in action"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-filters-emboss.docbook:32
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is an example of the emboss filter. The original image is (1) and the "
"transformed image is (2). The <guilabel>Depth</guilabel> applied is 10%."
msgstr ""

